                        "entry_id": "d72d24a0-5431-3ed3-98ee-99066a016cb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who nests."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d7691b0-f7a2-32a1-8ed6-6b71856a1aa2",
                        "entry_id": "d72d24a0-5431-3ed3-98ee-99066a016cb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who forms a strong attachment to their home."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "603c5b35-f35b-47e4-bc0f-8a2d2e00acda",
                                "sense_id": "4d7691b0-f7a2-32a1-8ed6-6b71856a1aa2",
                                "text": "I suppose, even for a nester, which I most assuredly am, there comes a time for moving on, and the time has finally come for my sother and me to leave Boston's Back Bay for other, not necessarily greener pastures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72b01c8c-2fa5-4174-ab4b-7c4fa0e53e0c",
                                "sense_id": "4d7691b0-f7a2-32a1-8ed6-6b71856a1aa2",
                                "text": "I AM A NESTER. I love our house and the things that fill it. My problem is, I am always on the go, rarely getting the opportunity to be there."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "46ce6ff4-696d-3def-950e-8171a133b37d",
                        "entry_id": "d72d24a0-5431-3ed3-98ee-99066a016cb5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who intends to settle in an area without permanent residents; a settler, as distinct from an explorer or pioneer."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da637269-372a-4022-bdc9-c717e6e9f43a",
                                "sense_id": "46ce6ff4-696d-3def-950e-8171a133b37d",
                                "text": "As cow camps were succeeded by the nesters, and towns came to grow at their sites, the springs continued to serve mankind both in an industrial way and as a playground for the ever-increasing population."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
